`startChangeDetection()` warms up the module graph by calling `server.warmupRequest()` for every story entry. In large repos this can mean thousands of requests and noticeably slow down dev-server startup. Consider limiting warmup (e.g. only story files, batched/throttled, or an opt-in feature flag), or switching to a strategy that doesn't require eagerly warming every story to begin emitting module-graph updates.
```suggestion
  // Warm up the module graph for a limited number of story files by default.
  // This avoids sending thousands of warmup requests in large repos, which can
  // significantly slow down dev-server startup.
  const entries = Object.values(storyIndex.entries);
  const warmAllStories = process.env.STORYBOOK_VITE_WARMUP_ALL_STORIES === 'true';
  const maxWarmupStoriesEnv = process.env.STORYBOOK_VITE_MAX_WARMUP_STORIES;
  const maxWarmupStories =
    maxWarmupStoriesEnv && !Number.isNaN(Number(maxWarmupStoriesEnv))
      ? Number(maxWarmupStoriesEnv)
      : 50;
  const warmupEntries = warmAllStories ? entries : entries.slice(0, maxWarmupStories);

  if (!warmAllStories && entries.length > warmupEntries.length) {
    logger.info(
      `Vite builder: warming module graph for ${warmupEntries.length} of ${entries.length} stories ` +
        `(set STORYBOOK_VITE_WARMUP_ALL_STORIES=true or STORYBOOK_VITE_MAX_WARMUP_STORIES to adjust)`
    );
  }

  await Promise.all(warmupEntries.map((entry) => server.warmupRequest(entry.importPath)));
```
